cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Principles of Synthetic Biology: course materials for UC Berkeley BioE 147/247"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arkin
    given-names: Adam P.
    affiliation: "University of California, Berkeley and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArkinLaboratory/posb2026"
abstract: >-
  Lectures, executable Jupyter notebooks, problem sets, and a small Python
  package for a one-semester course on the design of synthetic biological
  systems. Covers circuit design principles (mass action, regulation functions,
  phase-plane analysis, bistability, feedforward loops, oscillation, noise, the
  digital abstraction) and engineering design under real host constraints
  (resource competition, constraint-based metabolic design, retroactivity,
  feedback control, evolutionary stability, communities, minimal cells,
  therapeutic circuits, generative design, and biosecurity).
keywords:
  - synthetic biology
  - systems biology
  - gene circuits
  - mathematical modeling
  - computational biology
  - education
license: CC-BY-4.0   # content; code in posb/, tools/, tests/ is BSD-3-Clause
version: "2026.1"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
